       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and 2,400 mg/day is the usual practical ceiling. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Some possible intended orders:\n\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want the dose as written, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I'll add a note to the order. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
