     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any adult indication or protocol that supports it. The extra risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is serious, and more dose won't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect beyond the usual ceiling.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily are common choices. I can enter either right away.\n- **Use a different agent or add one.** If the goal is stronger symptom control, another drug or a multimodal approach would be safer than going above the ibuprofen ceiling.\n- **Go through pharmacy and the attending.** If there is a specialty protocol I'm not aware of, pharmacy or the attending can review and enter it directly. That is the right route for a dose outside labeled limits.\n\nTell me if you want me to enter one of the in-range regimens."
      }
     ],
